## End-to-End Flow (How Everything Fits Together)

```
Client (curl / browser)
  ↓
src/routes/index.ts          → URL matcher, mounts /api/*
  ↓
Controller (thin)            → validates input, delegates
  ↓
Service (business logic)     → vector math, embeddings, nearest neighbour
  ↓
Services (data)              → corpus of sentences, vector arithmetic examples
  ↓
Types (shared interfaces)    → Vector, SentenceEmbedding, Neighbor, AppConfig
  ↓
Config (env)                 → port, dim, etc.
  ↓
Express + errorHandler       → HTTP server, centralised error handling
  ↓
Client response (JSON)
```

## Commands

```bash
npm install        # Install all dependencies
npm run dev        # Run with tsx (no build needed)
npm run build      # Compile TypeScript to JavaScript in ./dist
npm start          # Run compiled server
```

## Quick Test Commands

```bash
# Health check
curl http://localhost:4000/api/health

# Show the build-target insight (paraphrases cluster vs word-overlap)
curl http://localhost:4000/api/similarity/chart

# Nearest neighbours for the fox sentence
curl "http://localhost:4000/api/neighbors?text=the%20quick%20brown%20fox%20jumps&top=3"

# All 4 similarity measures between two sentences
curl "http://localhost:4000/api/similarity?a=...&b=..."

# Vector arithmetic: king - man + woman ≈ queen
curl http://localhost:4000/api/vector-arithmetic

# Full corpus
curl http://localhost:4000/api/sentences
```

## Notes on the Implementation

- **No external embedding API needed** — the app uses a deterministic hash-based
  vector generator so it runs anywhere without API keys.
- **TypeScript strict mode** — `tsconfig.json` has `"strict": true`.
- **ES modules** — `package.json` has `"type": "module"`, so all imports use `.js` extensions.
- **Express 5** — the app targets Express 5.x features (error-handling middleware, etc.).
